@page {
    route: "/error-demo/",
    draft: Bool.false,
    theme: "rocci",
    color_scheme: "dark",
    meta: {
        title: "rocci error pages",
        description: "404, parse, and compile diagnostics while rocci run is serving",
    },
}

@css {
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
        background:
            radial-gradient(circle at 78% 8%, rgba(55, 242, 159, 0.13), transparent 31rem),
            linear-gradient(145deg, var(--rd-color-bg) 0%, var(--rd-color-bg) 55%, var(--rd-color-surface) 100%);
    }
}

@component
DemoLinks = |{}| {
    @css {
        .demo-links {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 0.65rem;
            margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
        }
        .demo-links a {
            display: inline-flex;
            padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
            border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--rd-color-accent) 28%, transparent);
            border-radius: 999px;
            background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--rd-color-accent) 10%, transparent);
            color: var(--rd-color-accent);
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            font-weight: 650;
            text-decoration: none;
        }
        .demo-links a:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
    }
    <p class="demo-links">
        <a href="/missing">Missing route</a>
        <a href="/error-demo">Slash redirect</a>
    </p>
}

# Error pages

`rocci run` keeps the preview open when a request misses, a template fails to
parse, or Roc rejects generated code. This page is the happy path so you can
click into a 404 without stopping the server.

## 404

`/missing` is not registered, so the fallback lists every route.

`/error-demo` and `/error-demo/` are different URLs (relative links resolve from
a different base), but they are the same page here. GET `/error-demo` answers
**308** to the registered `/error-demo/` form and keeps the query string. Both
forms stay distinct if you register each. Set
`http.redirect_trailing_slash = false` in `rocci.toml` to 404 with a hint
instead.

<DemoLinks />

## Parse error

Parse examples live in their own directory so they cannot take this page down.
From the repo root:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/errors/parse/Broken.rocdown
```

That still opens the window. The page is the diagnostic, with a source frame
instead of `template compilation failed`.
